import BlindLedger.Sha3Quick

/-! Faster permutation for `Sha3Quick.lean`.  `Quick.perm` is a loop over twelve double rounds that does Nat arithmetic and
    an array read for its round constants each step; those carry overflow calls that make the compiler spill the 25 lanes
    around them.  Here the loop walks a list of round constants (four per node, read as plain `UInt64` fields), so the
    loop body is only the rounds.  Same formulas, same stored (complemented) lanes; `permA_eq` in `Sha3LanesEq.lean`
    proves it equal to `Quick.perm permSteps`.  `rounds4` is four rounds on the 25 lanes; a caller that carries the lanes
    as arguments (`steps` here, `run` in `Gate/Engine3/Sha3Range.lean`) reads the result's fields at once, so the compiler
    never builds the state object. -/
namespace BlindLedger.Semantic
namespace Lanes

open Quick

/-- Round constants, four to a node. -/
inductive Rc where
  | nil : Rc
  | cons (r0 r1 r2 r3 : UInt64) (tl : Rc) : Rc

